{
  "name": "Daily solar & battery permits with contractor phone -> Google Sheets + Slack (Apify)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily solar & battery permits -> Google Sheets + Slack\n\n**What it does:** every morning at 07:00 it runs the Apify Actor *Building Permit Leads + Contractor Phone* (`RickyZ1X~building-permits-contractor-leads`) for Austin TX, San Diego CA and NYC DOB, keeps only NEW solar / battery-storage permits that have a contractor phone, appends them to Google Sheets and posts a one-message Slack digest.\n\n### Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. **Apify token**: Apify Console -> Settings -> API & Integrations -> copy your personal API token. In the *Run Apify Actor* node create a **Header Auth** credential: Name = `Authorization`, Value = `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_API_TOKEN`.\n2. In the node URL, replace `RickyZ1X` with the Actor owner's username shown on the Store page.\n3. **Google Sheets**: create a sheet whose first row has exactly these headers: `Issued, City, State, Categories, Solar kW, Battery kWh, Contractor, Phone, License, Address, Description, Source URL`. Paste the sheet ID (from its URL) into *Append to Google Sheet* and pick the tab.\n4. **Slack**: connect a Slack credential and set the channel in *Post Slack digest*.\n5. Click **Test workflow** once, then **Activate**.\n\n### Cost\nRuns are billed to *your* Apify account per event (`permit-record`, plus `contact-enriched-record` for rows with a contractor phone). `maxTotalRecords` in the request body caps the spend per run. The Apify free plan's monthly credit is enough to try it. `onlyNew: true` means you only pay for permits you have not received before.\n\n### Notes\n- `run-sync-get-dataset-items` waits up to 300 s. For large pulls (many sources / long `daysBack`), switch to the async run endpoint + a dataset fetch.\n- Edit `sources` / `categories` in the JSON body (sources: austin_tx, san_diego_ca, nyc_dob, seattle_wa, los_angeles_ca, chicago_il; categories: solar, battery_storage, roofing, hvac, ev_charger, adu, pool).\n\n### Compliance\nB2B use only. Data comes from official public open-data permit feeds and contains **no homeowner names or homeowner contact data**; phones are the contractor's business numbers as filed on permits. You (the user) are responsible for complying with the TCPA, the National Do-Not-Call Registry, state telemarketing / mini-TCPA laws and CAN-SPAM before contacting anyone.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "5e1f2a10-0001-4c1a-9b10-a0a0a0a00001",
